# Post-mortem -- slice 0160, attempt 03

## Summary

The normal profile-1 resume of 0160 stopped right after its worker exited, before any gate or review, with "executability receipt is stale: semantic source, prompt or validator changed".
The only stale input is `.specrc`: its `agent` key was switched from `openai-codex` to `claude-code` at 17:03:11Z, 43 seconds into the live worker round. The product, the plan and the 0160 repair are all unchanged.

## Root cause

Owner: **an operator action**. Someone edited `.specrc` outside the arc while the arc was running. The receipt binds that whole file. ASG `executability/receipt.py:input_fingerprint` (line 70) records `"specrc": file_hash(repo_root / ".specrc")`. `validate_receipt` (lines 107-108) reports any difference as the message above. The runner re-validates after every worker exit (`multistep/_arc_runner/runtime/run_arc_runner.py:4424-4427`) and stops through `_stop_reliability` (4010-4025) before the build gate. Boot had passed because the pre-emit `compile_spec` re-publishes the receipt from the current inputs at every launch (`step_compiler/compile.py:1510-1515`, called from `multistep/_common/runtime/main.py:278-284` ahead of the boot check at `run_arc_runner.py:2653-2667`). The receipt written at 17:02:14 therefore carried the old `.specrc` hash. The edit landed at 17:03:11, and the post-worker check at 17:05:58 caught it. I recomputed the fingerprint read-only with ASG's own functions. Every source, prompt, validator and bundle hash matches, and so do all 988 compiled hashes. Only `specrc` differs. `cleaned_sha256` normalizes line endings, so the CRLF now in the working `.specrc` is not the cause. The changed `agent` value is.

The worker did not make the edit: its impl-log and state-of-the-world both record it as a concurrent change it left alone. ASG writes `.specrc` only in doctor fixes that add blocks or bump `data_version`, and none of them sets `agent`. The rule that fired behaved the same way at the green path. The arc's previous agent switch (`98a2f57`, `0050-0035-manual`, 2026-11-05 22:33Z, `claude-code` → `openai-codex`) was made with the arc stopped and committed before the next boot (log 2083). That boot re-published the receipt, and no stop followed. The two cases differ only in when the edit was made. This is not a repeat of the 0069 stale-receipt stop: that one was a tool defect in registry initialization, fixed under ASG 0090 manual 030 (`ASG-ERRORS.md:55`). It is not a repeat of 0160-01 (schema contradiction, manual 012) or 0160-02 (elevation scope, manual 013) either. Both of those repairs are committed in `37cb549` and remain valid. One tool weakness, not causal: the message names neither `.specrc` nor `agent`. The receipt also binds dispatch-only keys that the spawner otherwise reads live: postmortem 03 was spawned on Anthropic from the edited file. The operator may file both as an ASG hardening. Neither is needed for recovery.

